# Chrome vs TfL brand

Two visual systems share this repo. Do not collapse them into a generic shadcn/Vercel dashboard look.

Canonical detail: [docs/design-system.md](docs/design-system.md) and Foundations IA.

## Split responsibility

| Surface | Language | Examples |
|---------|----------|----------|
| **Site chrome** | shadcn / base-nova semantic tokens | Sidebar, docs layout, buttons, cards, callouts, install command UI |
| **Domain / product visuals** | TfL brand + diagram tokens | Line colours, roundels, line/branch strips, status severity treatments, station labels |

```tsx
// ✅ Chrome — semantic tokens
<aside className="bg-sidebar text-sidebar-foreground border-sidebar-border">

// ✅ Domain — TfL tokens / brand helpers
import { UNDERGROUND_LINE_COLOURS, DIAGRAM_SCALE_CLASS } from "@/lib/tfl/brand";
<div className={DIAGRAM_SCALE_CLASS} style={{ color: UNDERGROUND_LINE_COLOURS.victoria }}>
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — zinc/Geist SaaS palette as “TfL UI”
<div className="bg-zinc-950 text-zinc-100 font-[Geist]">
  <div className="rounded-xl bg-gradient-to-br from-purple-500 to-indigo-600">
```

## No card chrome by default (domain components)

TfL / library components ship **without** outer border, border-radius, or card padding. Consumers wrap in their own `Card` (or none) when they want a framed surface.

Badges and chips also default to **square corners** (`rounded-none` / no `rounded-*`). Do not add `rounded-md` / `rounded-full` on line or bus route chips unless the consumer opts in via `className`.

```tsx
// ✅ Component is the content; page owns layout
<div className="grid md:grid-cols-12 gap-8">
  <div className="md:col-span-8">
    <ArrivalsBoard data={…} stopName="Oxford Circus" />
  </div>
</div>

// ❌ Don't bake a card into the library component
<div className="rounded-2xl border p-6">
  <ArrivalsBoard … />
</div>
```

Bus route chips (`BusNumberChip`): TfL bus red (`TFL_MODAL_COLOURS.buses`), fixed `w-[5ch]`, no horizontal padding, `text-box: trim-both cap alphabetic` for optical center (route codes ≤ 4 characters). Mixed-line arrivals row chips (`LineBadge` 3-letter / `LineBadgeGroup variant="codes"`) use the same `w-[5ch]` box. Platform chips share the same cap text-box trim — casing stays as written, not forced uppercase.

## Beautiful defaults (chrome only)

For docs chrome and app shell:

- Prefer `style: base-nova` already configured in `components.json`  
- Use CSS variables / semantic utilities: `bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `text-muted-foreground`, `border-border`, `bg-primary`, `ring-ring`  
- One density per page (comfortable or compact); do not mix arbitrary padding scales  
- Lucide icons at consistent sizes (`size-4` / `size-5`)  
- Cards are for **interaction or docs grouping**, not decorative wrappers around every paragraph  
- Domain components ship without outer card chrome (border / radius / padding); see “No card chrome by default” above

Do **not** default the product to dark mode + Geist because the shadcn/Vercel skill suggests it for dashboards. This site is content- and brand-led; respect existing theme (`next-themes`, P22 Underground as the site default when the Adobe kit is configured).

## TfL domain rules

- **Do not** download or redistribute Johnston. P22 Underground (Adobe Fonts) is this site’s Johnston-like default. Hammersmith One is the free fallback. Neither is Johnston.  
- Line / mode colours come from `@/lib/tfl/brand` (Issue 4 tokens), not ad-hoc hex in JSX unless matching a documented token.  
- Roundel and trademark behaviour: follow Foundations constants (`ROUNDEL_*`, licensing copy on Foundations pages).  
- Site favicon / apple-icon: grey filled placeholder roundel — not line-colour bars, not the trademarked mark. See [site-favicon.mdc](site-favicon.mdc).
- Diagram geometry ratios live in `LINE_DIAGRAM` / strip components — not in theme `--radius` tokens.  
- Station labels: use `StationName` / `formatStationLabel`; never ad-hoc `<br>` hacks for diagram names.
- Arrivals board tiles: fixed rhythm + absolute hairlines / box-border brand bars — see [docs/design-system.md](docs/design-system.md) (“Arrivals board rhythm”) and [`.cursor/rules/arrivals-board-layout.mdc`](arrivals-board-layout.mdc).

## Homepage and Blocks proof

The proof surface should read as **London transport**, not as a shadcn marketing bento:

- Status boards, line strips, arrivals, maps — yes  
- Generic finance charts, QR “Ledger”, AI chat chrome as the brand story — no  
- Restrained chrome around loud TfL colour and schematic structure — yes  
- Homepage demos are proof, not hit-targets — discovery CTA in the hero (e.g. Browse components), not overlay links on the boards  

## Motion

`motion` is available. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`. Prefer intentional motion on domain previews over decorative chrome animation.

## Anti-patterns

- Purple/indigo gradient themes, glassmorphism, glow stacks on docs chrome  
- Nested cards inside cards for MDX layout  
- Replacing TfL line colours with a single accent for “consistency” with shadcn  
- Teaching primitives with fake SaaS content instead of transport fixtures  
- Mixing `text-xs sm:text-sm` on diagram ticks/rings/labels (desyncs `--tfl-diagram-scale`)  
